      "message": "memblock_memsize_mod_kernel_size() which is not an __init_memblock function is using this variable which is marked as __initdata_memblock. You can\u0027t do that, the variable will be freed after init and memblock_memsize_mod_kernel_size() can be used after that. Presubmits correctly generate this error:\n\n```\nWARNING: modpost: vmlinux: section mismatch in reference: memblock_memsize_mod_kernel_size+0x13 (section: .text) -\u003e memblock_debug (section: .meminit.data)\nWARNING: modpost: vmlinux: section mismatch in reference: memblock_memsize_mod_kernel_size+0x29 (section: .text) -\u003e memsize_memap (section: .meminit.data)\nWARNING: modpost: vmlinux: section mismatch in reference: memblock_memsize_mod_reusable_size+0x13 (section: .text) -\u003e memblock_debug (section: .meminit.data)\nWARNING: modpost: vmlinux: section mismatch in reference: memblock_memsize_mod_reusable_size+0x29 (section: .text) -\u003e memsize_kinit (section: .meminit.data)\nERROR: modpost: Section mismatches detected.\nSet CONFIG_SECTION_MISMATCH_WARN_ONLY\u003dy to allow them.\n```",
